  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Wisconsin received $191M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 1,253 awards with an average award size of $152K. Obligations fell 96.1% year over year. Historical context shows larger prior-year totals: FY22 was $5.6B, FY23 was $5.7B, FY24 was $9.9B, FY25 was $7.4B, and FY26 was $4.9B. The FY2027 to date total is a partial fiscal-year figure. Health-related spending dominates the current-year mix, and the largest single buying agency is the Department of Veterans Affairs with $120M. The composition of top vendors and industries underscores a concentration in medical services and insurance-related work, with OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. and WISCONSIN PHYSICIANS SERVICE INSURANCE CORP. together accounting for a large share of obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is the current-year drop and what does that mean?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 96.1% year over year. FY2027 to date obligations are $191M compared with multi-billion totals in FY22 through FY26. The partial fiscal-year nature of the FY2027 figure matters because prior years show sustained, much larger spending levels. Watch buying-agency and vendor activity for the remainder of the fiscal year to see whether totals climb toward prior-year ranges."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top agencies and vendors in Wisconsin right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency with $120M. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $45.2M, and the General Services Administration follows with $9.9M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. leads vendors with $85.6M and WISCONSIN PHYSICIANS SERVICE INSURANCE CORP. follows with $41.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Wisconsin?",
      "a": "Wisconsin received $191M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 1,253 awards and an average award size of $152K. Prior fiscal years were much larger: FY22 $5.6B, FY23 $5.7B, FY24 $9.9B, FY25 $7.4B, and FY26 $4.9B. Note that the FY2027 total is a partial fiscal-year figure and obligations fell 96.1% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Wisconsin?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awarded $120M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services awarded $45.2M and the General Services Administration awarded $9.9M. Other top buying agencies include the Department of Agriculture at $7.2M and the Department of Justice at $4.8M. The remaining top-10 buying agencies each accounted for $2.4M or less."
    },
